# roxywi_letsencrypt (Resource)

Manage Let's Encrypt certificates.

## Example Usage

{{ tffile "./examples/resources/letsencrypt/example_1.tf" }}


<!-- schema generated by tfplugindocs -->
## Schema

### Required

- `domains` (List of String) Certificate domains; the first determines the PEM name.
- `server_id` (Number) The ID of the server to deploy to.
- `type` (String) What challenge should be used. Available: 'standalone', 'route53', 'digitalocean', 'cloudflare', 'linode'

### Optional

- `api_key` (String, Sensitive) Route53 access key ID. Conflicts with `dns_profile_id`.
- `api_token` (String, Sensitive) DNS API token; Route53 secret access key. Conflicts with `dns_profile_id`.
- `description` (String) Description of the certificate.
- `dns_profile_id` (Number) Existing DNS profile in the same group (Roxy-WI 9.1+).
- `draft` (Boolean) Save without issuing. Change to false to run preflight and issue. Default: false.
- `email` (String) Email address to use for registration with Let's Encrypt.
- `timeouts` (Block, Optional) (see [below for nested schema](#nestedblock--timeouts))

### Read-Only

- `id` (String) The ID of this resource.
- `status` (String) Certificate lifecycle status.
- `pem_name` (String) Managed PEM filename.
- `not_after` (String) Certificate expiry in UTC.
- `next_run_at` (String) Next renewal check in UTC.
- `retry_at` (String) Next automatic retry in UTC.
- `last_task_id` (Number) Latest Operations task ID.
- `last_error_code` (String) Latest certificate error code.
- `legacy_pending` (Boolean) Whether legacy cron migration is required.

